# Code comments

This is an Expo / React Native **app**, not an `expo-*` SDK package. Follow Expo’s “quality over quantity” and “explain the iceberg” (failures, side effects, platform quirks) — not TSDoc on every export. Expo’s `@param` / `@platform` / `@example` style is for generated API docs, not screens and stores.

Put a **1–2 sentence `//` comment immediately above** any non-obvious block: tricky control flow, workarounds, invariants, timing, caching, platform quirks, or anything a later reader would not infer from the names alone.

Use a short `/** … */` only when an export’s contract is not obvious from the name (side effects, import cycles, “do not call from X”).

Comment **why**, not what. Skip straightforward code (simple returns, obvious maps, standard hooks). Do not repeat TypeScript types in comments. Do not add file-level READMEs.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — narrates the next line
// Increment i by 1
i += 1;

// ❌ BAD — no comment on a non-obvious choice
setTimeout(() => flushResume(), 60_000);

// ✅ GOOD — why, placed above the block
// Persist on a 1-minute debounce so cloud writes stay off the playback tick.
setTimeout(() => flushResume(), 60_000);

// ✅ GOOD — export whose callers would otherwise create a cycle
/** Downloads call this via dynamic import so the two modules do not import each other statically. */
```
